# SCARF

> SCARF is the Samoyed Club of America Education and Research Foundation, funding research and publishing health information for Samoyed owners and breeders.

## Diseases

- [Diseases](/diseases.md): The site's disease section for Samoyed owners, breeders, and veterinarians.
- [Diseases A–Z](/diseases/a-to-z-diseases.md): Index of the disorders, syndromes, and conditions covered on the site.
- [Hip Dysplasia (HD)](/diseases/hip-dysplasia-hd.md): Causes, signs, diagnosis, and treatment of hip dysplasia in Samoyeds.
- [Sebaceous Adenitis (SA)](/diseases/sebaceous-adenitis-sa.md): An overview of sebaceous adenitis, a skin disease seen in the breed.
- [Degenerative Myelopathy](/diseases/degenerative-myelopathy.md): Information on the progressive spinal cord disease and genetic testing.

## Owners

- [Owners](/owners.md): Health information for people who own or live with a Samoyed.
- [The healthy Samoyed](/owners/the-healthy-samoyed.md): Puppy, senior, vaccination, nutrition, and first-aid guidance.
- [Health problems](/owners/health-problems.md): How to recognise and respond to common health problems.
- [Selecting a Samoyed puppy](/owners/selecting-a-samoyed-puppy.md): What to look for when choosing a puppy and a breeder.

## Breeders

- [Breeders](/breeders.md): Health and breeding information for Samoyed breeders.
- [Genetics](/breeders/genetics.md): Inheritance, testing, and genetic disease in the breed.
- [Breeding](/breeders/breeding.md): Practical guidance for planning and raising a litter.

